From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: blurbery <271863866+blurbery@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ad_spdif: carry E-AC-3 at four times the codec rate

IEC 61937 carries each E-AC-3 frame of 1536 samples in a burst of 6144
carrier frames, so the carrier rate is four times the codec rate. Upstream
opens every E-AC-3 stream at 192000 Hz, which is only right for streams
coded at 48 kHz: with a 44.1 kHz stream, mpv's audio timestamps run about
9% fast.

When the spdif muxer is built for E-AC-3, use four times the codec rate
cached for the stream (4 x 48000 when it is unknown) for both the muxer's
stream rate and the output frame format. AC-3 keeps upstream's behaviour
(carrier rate = codec rate, 48000 when unknown), the channel count stays 2
and no log line is added. The AVFoundation audio output divides the carrier
rate by 4 again to time passthrough, so the two must agree.

Applies to mpv v0.41.0 with upstream commit 1388a453 (patch 0001), whose
cached codec rate it uses.

